    "chapter": "07 结构体与内存",
    "cReference": "#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <string.h>\n#include <stddef.h>\n#include <limits.h>\ntypedef struct{int exists;long long stamp,value;}Record;int main(void){int n,channel;long long stamp,value;Record r[101]={{0,0,0}};if(scanf(\"%d\",&n)!=1)return 0;for(int i=0;i<n;i++){if(scanf(\"%d%lld%lld\",&channel,&stamp,&value)!=3)return 0;if(!r[channel].exists||stamp>=r[channel].stamp){r[channel].exists=1;r[channel].stamp=stamp;r[channel].value=value;}}int any=0;for(int c=1;c<=100;c++)if(r[c].exists){any=1;printf(\"%d %lld %lld\\n\",c,r[c].stamp,r[c].value);}if(!any)puts(\"EMPTY\");return 0;}\n",
    "oracleNotes": "Python dictionary stores each channel winner under (timestamp,input-index) ordering, independent from indexed C records."
  }
